@page "/platform"

@*
    Standalone portal page hosting the platform stats section (issue #1692). Kept as its own route
    so the stats panel is fully additive - it does not alter the agent dashboard or chat surface -
    while still being reachable in the portal at /platform.

    The panel carries no chrome of its own (Home's .home-summary supplies the bar there), so this
    page wraps it in the shared .stats-bar. And it opens the loop list by default: this route exists
    to answer "what is running right now", and it was spending a whole viewport to say "0" four
    times while the only substantive content sat behind a disclosure click.
*@

<PageTitle>BotNexus &mdash; Platform</PageTitle>

<div class="platform-config-page">
    <header class="platform-config-toolbar">
        <h2 class="page-heading"><Icon Name="activity" Size="24" /><span>Platform</span></h2>
    </header>

    <div class="config-page">
        <div class="config-panel-canvas">
            <div class="stats-bar" data-testid="platform-stats-bar">
                <PlatformStatsPanel LoopsInitiallyExpanded="true" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
